-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 [ about ]
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  BBSFirewall is a lightweight TCP proxy firewall for retro BBS systems.
  Drop it in front of your BBS and it'll handle the riff-raff so you
  don't have to babysit port 23 at 2am.

  Written in Node.js. Runs anywhere Node runs. No drama.

  https://github.com/SysopNetwork/BBSFirewall

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 [ features ]
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * TCP proxy — forwards telnet connections to your backend BBS
  * Per-IP connection limiting — because some people have no chill
  * HTTP redirect — send web browsers somewhere useful instead of nowhere
  * GeoIP country blocking — MaxMind GeoLite2, works offline
  * IP whitelist — trusted IPs bypass everything, no questions asked
  * IP blocklist — permanent bans with CIDR support
  * Rate limiting — flood protection with auto-temporary blocks
  * SSH server — accepts any credentials, proxies to telnet backend
  * UTF-8 / CP437 detection — routes clients to the right backend port
  * Graceful shutdown — cleans up nicely when you tell it to stop

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 [ setup ]
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  1. npm install
  2. cp .env.example .env  (and edit it)
  3. npm run setup-geoip   (optional, for country blocking)
  4. npm start

  Full docs in README.md

